{center}{arial}By Order of Her Majesty
{center}Gloria Magna Regina
{center}Queen of Normos

{center}{arialbld}Eleanor-IV{arial}{pause}


To {rank} {name},{pause}


We were greatly disappointed by your disobedience and we hold that a sentence by the Administrative Court of Defence of three days of prison for insubordination is sufficient punishment for such an immature attitude.{pause}

Nevertheless rebelliousness is the first act which characterises a future leader, ardour and recklessness are distinctive of youth and such trivial acts must be forgiven to a young person who succeeds in surviving them. This is the reason why, by virtue of our powers of mercy, we indemnify you of these punishments.{pause}

Having thus implicated our royal person in judging that the courageous acts which were your own were not of simple stupidity blessed by luck, I dare to believe that you will honour the favour of our arbitration by adopting in time a conduct more becoming to your new appointments.{pause}

Indeed it is another of our privileges which we employ with great happiness when the occasion presents itself, and unfortunately these are extremely rare.{pause}

We name you Knight of the Order of Valour.{pause}

And, to you from me {name}, give me the pleasure of staying alive, you are more useful to us as a hero than as a martyr.{pause}



{offset125}{date}

{offset150}Of Normland, the Sovereign

{offset175}{arialbld}Eleanor the Fourth{arial}

{offset50}{award11}{offset0}


